From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strata-2080Ti stack <stack@noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:10:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] QWEN-OVERLAP-Costruisce e conta la seconda ipotesi di B
 (STRATA_OV_TREE=1) senza lanciarla

La diagnostica del 20/10 dice seconda scelta giusta 45,2% (seriale) / 29,5% (pipeline): sopra la soglia di
segnalazione, quindi la B ad albero si avvia come lavoro a livelli, tutti dietro STRATA_OV_TREE (0 spento = oggi,
byte identico). Livello 1 qui: quando make_b costruisce B dalla catena, viene costruita anche una seconda ipotesi
per la stessa riga 0 - il runner-up della catena su quella posizione (chain_top2/chain_top2_prob, la strada dei
logit che scendono in host dentro il grafo di ogni passo: per questo STRATA_OV_TREE accende anche ov_top2_stat,
che e l'unico modo per far arrivare in host il secondo candidato) - con i draft della catena dopo, p_on = pa *
p(secondo) e gli stessi guardi di B (niente finestre lookup/suffix, niente su un rollback pending). NON viene
lanciata: pump0 e i lanci conoscono solo A, B e D, quindi le finestre servite e i token emessi restano quelli di
oggi.

Al verdetto, per ogni finestra accettata intera con una seconda ipotesi: prima scelta giusta / seconda giusta /
nessuna, piu' quante seconde ipotesi passerebbero la soglia theta e la p_on media delle due. Riga di fine
richiesta (con STRATA_DECODE_TIMING): "strata overlap tree (STRATA_OV_TREE=1): ...".

Livelli 2 (una terza corsia di verifier) e 3 (il lancio e la scelta) non sono fatti qui: la nota di design in
OVERLAP_2026-10-19.md dice perche' due finestre speculative sullo stesso stadio chiedono una terza verifier per
stadio e un terzo buffer di snapshot GDN.

Compilato si' (build_lock_noeng.py --bench-held, rc 0, sha256 a1bedd81, 20 s incrementale, log
corse_2080ti/20261019_overlap/build3.log), installato no, provato no, misurato no. Nessuna GPU toccata, strata.exe
del servizio 8100 mai fermato, bench.lock non cancellato.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Follow-ups squashed into this patch:
- bf03aeac QWEN-OVERLAP-Da' una corsia in piu' al loop in pipeline per la seconda ipotesi (STRATA_OV_TREE=2)

diff --git a/include/strata/core/mtp.hpp b/include/strata/core/mtp.hpp
index d0d8841f..1d76b2dc 100644
--- a/include/strata/core/mtp.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/core/mtp.hpp
@@ -157,7 +157,12 @@ public:
     /// lab/overlap 1.2 (`STRATA_OV_TOP2_STAT=1`, a diagnostic, opt-in and slow): the chain step's runner-up under the
     /// draft head and its probability -- what a tree draft's second branch would have to hit.  Each step's logits are
     /// copied to the host inside its own graph; -1 / 0 when the switch is off or the step has no second token.
+    /// lab/overlap 1.6 (`STRATA_OV_TREE=1..3`): the tree draft needs the same runner-up on the live path, so the tree's
+    /// switch turns this data path on too (the copy node is the only way the second candidate reaches the host).
     static bool ov_top2_stat();
+    /// lab/overlap 1.6: the tree draft's level (0 off, 1 build and score the second hypothesis, 2 its verifier exists,
+    /// 3 it is launched).  Read once, like every other STRATA_ switch.
+    static int ov_tree();
     int32_t chain_top2(int j) const { return j >= 0 && j < 8 ? chain_top2_[j] : -1; }
     float chain_top2_prob(int j) const { return j >= 0 && j < 8 ? chain_top2_prob_[j] : 0.0f; }
 
diff --git a/src/core/mtp.cpp b/src/core/mtp.cpp
index e1e1c9db..2b2d6e87 100644
--- a/src/core/mtp.cpp
+++ b/src/core/mtp.cpp
@@ -548,8 +548,21 @@ void MtpDrafter::record_top2(int j) {
 // A chain step's draft logits (the row `row_top_prob` took its top-1 and its probability from) also come to the host,
 // so a window's verdict can ask what the drafter's runner-up was at the bonus position: the token a tree draft's
 // second branch would have to hit.  Off: no pinned staging, no copy node, the round and step graphs are the old ones.
+// lab/overlap 1.6 (STRATA_OV_TREE=1..3): the tree draft's level.  1 = the second hypothesis for a speculative
+// window's row 0 is built from the chain's runner-up and scored at the verdict (nothing is launched: the tokens stay
+// the ones of today); 2 = its verifier on the first card exists (its arena, graphs, hand-off and snapshot are made);
+// 3 = it is launched speculatively beside the first one and the verdict keeps the branch whose row 0 is right.
+int MtpDrafter::ov_tree() {
+    static const int v = [] { const char* e = std::getenv("STRATA_OV_TREE"); return e != nullptr ? std::atoi(e) : 0; }();
+    return v;
+}
+
 bool MtpDrafter::ov_top2_stat() {
-    static const bool on = [] { const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_OV_TOP2_STAT"); return v != nullptr && std::atoi(v) != 0; }();
+    // The runner-up's data path: the diagnostic asks for it, and the tree draft cannot pick a second branch without it.
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_OV_TOP2_STAT");
+        return (v != nullptr && std::atoi(v) != 0) || ov_tree() > 0;
+    }();
     return on;
 }
 
